{{liushu|p}} – a horn. A conservative version is [[𧢲]]. Similar but unrelated to [[甬]], [[用]], and the bottom part of [[備]].

===Etymology===
From {{inh|zh|sit-pro|*krəw||horn; angle; corner}} (STEDT). Cognate with {{cog|bo|རྭ||horn}}, {{cog|grt|grong||horn}}, {{cog|kac|nrung||horn}}, {{cog|cdm|रोङः|tr=roŋʔ|t=horn}}, {{och-l|觡|antler}}. The Tibeto-Burman ''*-ŋ'' final variant is reflected in {{och-l|觥|drinking vessel made from animal horn}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}). Possibly also related to {{och-l|鹿|deer}} ({{zh-ref|Sagart, 1999}}).

A derivative is {{och-l|餃|stuffed dumpling}}, named for its horn-like shape ({{zh-ref|Norman, 1988}}).

It is probably unrelated with {{noncog|ine-pro||*ḱr̥h₂nós|t=horn}} ( < {{m|ine-pro|*ḱerh₂-|t=horn}}) and {{noncog|sem-pro|*ḳarn-|t=horn}} despite the phonological and semantic resemblance between the three.

